title: 'The question splits in two: what changed, and what this subscription covers.'
pid: 60894c2b-4631-4197-bf40-410b8f5caa84
body: |2-
  What changed since some baseline is a property of the author's
  skgrepo. That is the diff problem, Vic's, and Ed's first wish ("show
  me what changed in someone else's skgrepo") is that alone. What a
  subscription covers, its region, is mine. The deep count is their
  intersection.
  Count from the changes upward, not from the subscribee downward.
  Changes are usually few (Ed's week of Jeff's: 23 files); a
  subscribee's subtree can be thousands of nodes. From each changed
  node walk containerward, crediting each node on the way, until the
  subscribee. That gives every level its own count too, so a reader can
  descend by the numbers, depth first, as Jeff means to read.
